# Copy to deploy/aitagger/.env (git-ignored) and adjust. Compose reads it automatically.

# Where the tagger container keeps its model files:
#   <AITAGGER_CACHE>/hub  WD EVA02-Large + PixAI Tagger v1.0 + RAM++ weights (tagger container, /cache; about 6 GB:
#                         1.4 GB WD, 1.9 GB PixAI, 3.0 GB RAM++, plus the converted fp16 WD model next to hub)
# Default when unset: ~/vlm/models/aitagger. An absolute path is the safest value here.
AITAGGER_CACHE=/home/youruser/vlm/models/aitagger

# The panel derives these from its settings and passes them when it starts the container; the values below are
# the defaults for starting by hand (measured on an RTX 4090, see docs/AI-TAGGER.md, "Measured (v3)").
# AITAGGER_VRAM_GB=5      # memory cap of the tagger process (WD + PixAI + RAM++); about 4.2 GB are used at 5. 4 works,
#                         # 3.5 is the lowest that loads (the micro-batches shrink, the speed does not), 3 does not
# AITAGGER_BATCH=8        # pictures per GPU micro-batch (PixAI is compute-bound: speed does not depend on it)
# IDLE_EXIT_MINUTES=20    # the tagger exits after this long without a request
